Rodman rule has been revised but the fight to keep stars in the NWSL goes o=
n


Gone are the eight criteria to be a High Impact Player so clubs can spend t=
heir money on whichever player they want =E2=80=93 and the solution makes s=
ense


The rule was informally named after Washington Spirit=E2=80=99s Trinity Rod=
man (left) after her protracted contract saga. Photograph: Jay Biggerstaff/=
NWSL/Getty Images


Megan Swanick


When Washington plays Chicago this Sunday in DC, =E2=80=9CRowdy Audi=E2=80=
=9D will probably be full. It will also be full when the post-season starts=
, should they lock up their top-four position with a positive result on Dec=
ision Day. Equipped with an accessible stadium in a big city, a proud fanba=
se, and a formidable roster rife with players qualifying for the High Impac=
t Player (HIP) rule=E2=80=99s initial criteria (including Trinity Rodman, w=
ho gave the rule its moniker), the Spirit hold sway in the attendance chart=
s.

But starting next season, everyone on the Spirit
https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTN=
tZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgrVZwi573h5aJedUKhFfwEmyhFprIKcaMeG2=
lYpVI9gZ42fWfW0fsygJHPKeAjc6oCWraquhmRe-HvMwH__1zyY5K3WidGv5TPylRTnlf3eREA4=
n2xAnT-N23FuQm5e-5sZwfhTfUeWwyr_Acg6WaHkqUO0KoKjyynURz7S-hwjmmOnDmnWazVPBRj=
IWClGJwKak59-LcCt_lbXVrog0TrkWHnHKTI3AZzpW21WkwPg-jc9Vzzi0pVkdFVHU60y9a/4va=
/JeTzbCquR6CLVrJq-Uq5uQ/t0/h001.TkODgchJnTnf_-KnYLCyGIElN3r7Ml4z3Z_fBntVIy4
will qualify for the =E2=80=9CRodman Rule=E2=80=9D
. So will every player in NWSL. Announced Friday, NWSL settled a grievance =
with the league=E2=80=99s Players Association, who argued that the initial =
criteria violated federal labor law.

Admittedly, when the new policy arrived on the scene last winter, it appear=
ed half-baked, a somewhat frantic attempt to keep Rodman from floating acro=
ss the Atlantic and doing something terrible, like playing for Michele Kang=
=E2=80=99s London City Lionesses instead of Michele Kang=E2=80=99s Washingt=
on Spirit.

A rule was born to prevent that. It allocated added funds beyond the salary=
 cap for players who met league-set criteria which clearly prioritized inte=
rnational name recognition in a global market. Qualifying players needed to=
 meet one of eight categories including SportsPro Media=E2=80=99s top 150 M=
ost Marketable Athletes (only Alessia Russo and Aitana Bonmat=C3=AD placed =
in 2026, though 16 female football players did in 2025, including three in =
the NWSL at the time =E2=80=93 Trinity Rodman, Sophia Wilson and Marta, in =
that order). It also included ESPN=E2=80=99s Top 50,
https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTN=
tZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEDom6Up7NBgS48fUZgZf5ceO-Bfvp-VHe3PDtb5mZUQQ-mEahIB-GXmRfP=
L0zNnc51hbTkHUwVqh4alpMRS2cG9EAuYufyu6yer66mmP15mCWJJ_7MQyHoiDs6iU3Tq0srIF5=
VCtZ6vBzI_9BQPwdk-b7RW4YRGbALPV9UV4VSJY4F0U4BIAERRVBVFOhMXPg_Pw5EvELkS2kBbI=
yxpWKq3tnm2HhzD2OzC1Lhbed2CScfZZpzBVoblJyCDWOrbFwd1z-5JWw4HMlZuqOgjOOUSORDs=
ab8o4h1OEWHAyrkY9A/4va/JeTzbCquR6CLVrJq-Uq5uQ/t1/h001.vSXQ9SpqEZujcvrGftaWT=
A6haQAKvuPnvQovlCkBf-U
the Guardian=E2=80=99s top 100
, top minutes on the US National Team, the Ballon d=E2=80=99Or=E2=80=99s 30=
-player list, or NWSL=E2=80=99s MVP and Best XI awards.

Some measure of umbrage followed, as invested onlookers argued for a more s=
imple solution: just raise the salary cap. And perhaps they should, but kee=
ping an American-style sports league competitive in a global football lands=
cape is less straightforward. The looming spectre of Europe=E2=80=99s super=
-teams, who have attracted key members of the USWNT starting XI, is ever pr=
esent, waiting to take Croix Bethune away for the right amount of money. No=
 doubt, the NWSL=E2=80=99s appeal is evident in its expansion and growth, i=
n the success of its spine of stateside stalwarts, in its rapidly expanding=
 dedicated facilities, and in the international talents such as Esme Morgan=
 or Ann-Katrin Berger that choose to sharpen their skills in the US.

However, the domestic sporting culture of the NWSL is somewhat at odds, in =
some ways a disadvantage, when it comes to maintaining its margins, with a =
stand-alone team structure in a parity-driven league, while competing for i=
nternational glory with teams such as Chelsea, Lyon or Barcelona, who spend=
 three times or more the amount that some NWSL teams do. While competing fo=
r status as the world=E2=80=99s go-to destination, for players and fans, gl=
ory hunting and name recognition do matter.

Just look at the Ballon d=E2=80=99Or: Barcelona=E2=80=99s women took all bu=
t one of the awards available to them, though Alexia Putellas, who
https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTN=
tZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgfixB8L8oyfwfaY5z-TlkJ0fQOEY3X-xfywO=
zWXdCv1IJz5GM6gs9ERIw1zpJk0JbHWms-qtos-m4bIUTXBOrJI1DBY4MBs4QUD0aMeVf43pQwb=
