<td valign=3D"top"><span style=3D"font-size:24px;font-style:italic;font-fam=
ily:Georgia, serif;font-weight:400;line-height:140%;color:#0077B6">Pablo Ig=
lesias Maurer</span></td>
<td width=3D"110" height=3D"90" style=3D"line-height:0;font-size:0"><img sr=
c=3D"https://i.guim.co.uk/img/uploads/2026/05/28/Pablo_Mauerer.png?quality=
=3D85&amp;dpr=3D2&amp;width=3D120&amp;s=3D9d33231f94bfbe49b35556b7c92aa264"=
 alt=3D"Pablo Iglesias Maurer" width=3D"110" height=3D"90"></td>
</tr></table></td></tr>
<tr><td style=3D"border-top:2px dashed;border-top-color:#999999;background-=
color:#FFFFFF;padding-bottom:8px">=C2=A0</td></tr>
<tr><td align=3D"left" class=3D"text" style=3D"background:#FFFFFF;font-size=
:0px;padding:0 16px;word-break:break-word;"><div style=3D"font-family:Georg=
ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">For years, the crisp air and changing colo=
rs of October brought forth a host of wonderful memories for <a href=3D"htt=
ps://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ=
7fIEMgszcCSneHEBwGTvREh8dEFBZ7Fmax2TIhC7LowobZO1kABZF38U2ks-qtu3q-m4OG6N_8f=
3okCzsPvKU1Rj45CphxklCqOSIxQ039o3uHckXSRHeiq4zV6Uithi_JebGjIeZn3CcrQob9n0MW=
wXzZ3MKZ9sVkbINgzJsK2TQGPedUE5tfOnkJfq_j2k5rlHNvvuKz0MLCexq4vhU2NLW4-7lR19D=
X-tqeTvSpjFwZ1jHMkM6Gn3HZg/4va/JeTzbCquR6CLVrJq-Uq5uQ/h9/h001.gG_LRLA7xPXPs=
hfFB_ooel5dVsSd_zIFX9xy54C_BUA" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">DC United</a> fan=
s =E2=80=93 visions of Eddie Pope heading home the winner in <a href=3D"htt=
ps://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ=
7fIEMgszcCSneHEBVF8zUl_OwycfjWF7OhNX1j_posZOAqd71WCLdyFPrywFUgXm4AlpGvDTXkY=
XXT-zvKq2uNT5UvXvlaLLJneV466vAXoRgW1ENLXXhIbJuv3RTRoyAOvdX90bUs_8exKcLVeXL_=
cQFpJsDTFOraEL9ZSY6DUEYzx1PFPM-eaSMJ8ti7xANF4GdKq48-PjKrD9cxFddzR0JANbG3_Uw=
HyvGvxwllwNm9F-s_uC6VHeewQ/4va/JeTzbCquR6CLVrJq-Uq5uQ/h10/h001._NkaSOBp3jRI=
EQYj1Sf2yNIyKwzI-J_yEZA7du-tLpA" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">Major League Soc=
cer</a>=E2=80=99s first-ever championship game, or Marco Etcheverry, Jaime =
Moreno and others tearing through defenders, helping establish MLS=E2=80=99=
s first true dynasty.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Nowadays, United fans have a different tra=
dition: hearing the team=E2=80=99s ownership apologize for yet another depr=
essing season and offer promises of a brighter future. With Wednesday night=
=E2=80=99s 2-1 loss to Toronto, United will now miss out on the playoffs fo=
r the seventh consecutive season =E2=80=93 in a league that lets at least 5=
0% of teams into the playoffs each year, with 60% of teams or more making i=
t in five of those seven years. If United fail to make it again next year, =
they=E2=80=99ll tie an all-time MLS record.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">United have cycled through coaches, player=
s and staff at a dizzying rate in recent years; their most recent attempt t=
o right the ship involved hiring Ren=C3=A9 Weiler, a Swiss journeyman who h=
as guided 10 clubs in a 20-year coaching career. United=E2=80=99s choice to=
 lead its sporting department felt even more bizarre: they hired Dr Erkut S=
ogut, a German-born lawyer and sports agent who had never worked in a front=
 office before, with Wikipedia saying he is =E2=80=9Cmost notable for being=
 the agent of football star Mesut =C3=96zil=E2=80=9D. Sogut =E2=80=93 who h=
as also penned a number of books about the =E2=80=9Chigh-octane=E2=80=9D wo=
rld of =E2=80=9Cfootball and the powerful agents who control it=E2=80=9D =
=E2=80=93 has yet to turn things around, even a little bit.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">United, who are seemingly too inept to per=
form the basic function of their business (fielding a competitive soccer te=
am) are nevertheless asking the DC government for hundreds of millions of d=
ollars to renovate Audi Field, their eight-year-old home.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">United are among the least ambitious teams=
 in MLS but they are far from the league=E2=80=99s only basket case. Below =
them at the bottom of the overall table are others straggling along for the=
ir own varied reasons: CF Montr=C3=A9al, Sporting KC and Atlanta United.</p=
>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">DC=E2=80=99s disastrous 2026 can=E2=80=99t=
 hold a candle this year to KC, whose misery started early, has continued a=
pace and has frequently bordered on the comical. The club was bounced out o=
f the US Open Cup at the first hurdle by USL side Colorado Springs Switchba=
cks in a 3-0 loss that could have been worse. On Wednesday night, the team =
lost 3-1 to Minnesota United to bring their goals conceded tally to an asto=
nishing 80 on the season, setting the league record with two games to go.</=
p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">KC were never going to do well this year. =
They opened preseason with just 17 players under contract and former Chicag=
o Fire and BSC Young Boys head coach Rapha=C3=ABl Wicky has thus far seemed=
 like an unsteady fit to say the least. It=E2=80=99s the kind of dynamic th=
at=E2=80=99s led the team to a place where their minutes leader is Calvin H=
arris, a forward who had mostly been an option off the bench in past MLS sp=
ots. Second on the minutes list is 24-year-old Wyatt Meyer, who went from r=
iding the bench and bouncing down to MLS Next Pro for Nashville in 2025 to =
anchoring 2026=E2=80=99s historically bad defense.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">There=E2=80=99s some room for optimism in =
Kansas City, at least, as there is at any team with a billionaire owner (th=
at is Peter Mallouk, who gained controlling owner status earlier this year)=
. The same can be said for Atlanta United, who are on the verge of missing =
the playoffs for the second consecutive year for the first time in franchis=
e history. It feels almost comical to worry about Atlanta, who have never b=
een short on ambition under Arthur Blank. That club spent millions to sign =
Miguel Almir=C3=B3n, Aleksei Miranchuk and Emmanuel Latte Lath and promptly=
 watched as each of them grossly underperformed. Latte Lath, a $22m transfe=
r from Middlesbrough, was arguably the biggest designated player bust in ML=
S history before Atlanta mercifully loaned him out to Union Berlin in Augus=
t.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Montreal haven=E2=80=99t won a match in a =
month and their fans rained pyrotechnics on the field and damaged stadium c=
oncourses after the team=E2=80=99s loss to Canadian Premier League side For=
ge FC in the Canadian Championship last weekend. Montreal, who have occasio=
nally been competitive and somehow remain somewhat relevant in their market=
, are also one of MLS=E2=80=99s longest-running shitshows, with owner Joey =
Saputo cycling through head coaches at a dizzying pace. Rumors of a sale =
=E2=80=93 or possible relocation =E2=80=93 have persisted for years.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The vibrance of Montreal as a soccer city,=
 and the team=E2=80=99s history of over three decades there, means faint ho=
pe remains that the team can turn things around. That=E2=80=99s true even a=
s the club bans fans from its stands in response to the aforementioned prot=
ests.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The tiny slivers of hope present in all of=
 these sides can not be found at this point for DC United, with supporters =
who have stuck by their club for nearly as long as those of Montreal. At th=
is point, barring them from the stands at Audi Field could be viewed as an =
act of love.</p>
