<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><em>In which the Guardian staff pick one g=
ame each day that we think is worth watching. Broadcast info is US and all =
times ET. Games for Monday to Wednesday will be covered in our Monday editi=
on.</em></p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><strong>Thursday: </strong>Fleetwood Town =
showed this week that cup upsets can still delight (unless, of course, you=
=E2=80=99re an Arsenal fan). In Spain, the Copa del Rey action features sev=
eral similarly lopsided matchups, but it may be worth keeping an eye on Dep=
ortivo A Coru=C3=B1a=E2=80=99s visit to sixth-tier Auriense, a club founded=
 in 2020 now playing in their first-ever Copa del Rey. <em><strong style=3D=
"color: #0077B6; font-style: normal; font-weight: 700;">Auriense v Deportiv=
o A Coru=C3=B1a</strong></em> is at 4pm on ESPN+.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><strong>Friday: </strong>Elversberg and Am=
erican winger Cole Campbell have made a solid impression in the Bundesliga,=
 and on Friday they face a Mainz side who are right next to them, just belo=
w the league=E2=80=99s European places. <em><strong style=3D"color: #0077B6=
; font-style: normal; font-weight: 700;">Elversberg v Mainz</strong></em> i=
s at 3.30pm on Telemundo and FuboTV.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><strong>Saturday: </strong>What now for Ma=
nchester United? The team are in a state of crisis even as Michael Carrick =
has held on to the manager=E2=80=99s job, and on Saturday they face a stiff=
 test with a visit to Chelsea, who are aiming to get back into the top four=
. <em><strong style=3D"color: #0077B6; font-style: normal; font-weight: 700=
;">Chelsea v Manchester United</strong></em> is at 8.30pm on USA and Telemu=
ndo.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><strong>Sunday:</strong> <em><strong style=
=3D"color: #0077B6; font-style: normal; font-weight: 700;">Liverpool v Arse=
nal</strong></em> (11.30am, Peacock and Telemundo) will attract plenty of e=
yeballs in the morning, but in the evening the best choice is going to be k=
eeping track of NWSL Decision Day =E2=80=93 the last day of the regular sea=
son where all the games are played at the same time. At stake this year: Go=
tham FC or San Diego Wave can win the NWSL Shield, and four teams are fight=
ing for one remaining spot in the playoffs. All the <em><strong style=3D"co=
lor: #0077B6; font-style: normal; font-weight: 700;">NWSL Decision Day</str=
ong></em> games kick off at 5pm on ESPN+, with Gotham v Utah Royals on ESPN=
.</p>
